# .NET Development Rules for Cline

You are an expert .NET developer. Apply the following rules when working on .NET projects.

## Project Structure
- Solution (`.sln`) at the repository root
- `src/` for production projects, `tests/` for test projects
- `Directory.Build.props`: `<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`, `<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>`, `<TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>`, `<TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>`
- `Directory.Packages.props`: `<ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>`

## C# Style
- `record` for DTOs and value objects
- Primary constructors for DI (`public class OrderService(IOrderRepository repo, ILogger<OrderService> logger)`)
- Switch expressions and `is` patterns over if/else chains
- Async methods: suffix with `Async`, accept `CancellationToken cancellationToken = default`
- Nullable enabled: annotate nullable returns with `?`
- Validation: `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull()`, `ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty()`
- Logging: use message templates — `logger.LogInformation("Order {OrderId} placed", orderId)` — never string interpolation

## Testing
Framework: xUnit + FluentAssertions + NSubstitute

- Test naming: `MethodName_StateUnderTest_ExpectedBehavior`
- AAA structure (Arrange / Act / Assert) with blank line separators
- `[Theory]` + `[InlineData]` for parameterised tests
- `Testcontainers` for integration tests with real databases

## ASP.NET Core API
- Minimal API with `MapGroup` (preferred for new services)
- `AddProblemDetails()` + `UseExceptionHandler()` for RFC 9457 error responses
- `AddHealthChecks()` with `/health/live` and `/health/ready` endpoints
- FluentValidation for request validation
- `IOptions<T>` for configuration binding

## Entity Framework Core
- Separate `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` classes applied via `ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly`
- `AsNoTracking()` for read-only queries
- Repository pattern; never call `SaveChangesAsync` from controllers
- Migrations: `dotnet ef migrations add <Name>` → `dotnet ef database update`

## Docker
- Multi-stage Dockerfile: `sdk` for build, `aspnet` for runtime
- Run as non-root user; expose port `8080`
- `ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:8080`

## Common Commands
```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build -c Release
dotnet test --collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"
dotnet ef migrations add <Name>
dotnet ef database update
dotnet format
dotnet list package --vulnerable
```
